+### Removing a user from an organization
+
+`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}` removes the user from every project of the
+organization and returns 204.
+
+- Only org admins may call it. Other members of the organization get 403.
+- The organization must be the caller's own, else 404. The user must belong to
+  that organization, else 404.
+- Removal applies to archived projects too (the one exception to the archived
+  rule above), so that offboarding does not fail on them.
+- Tasks in those projects that are assigned to the user are unassigned, so no
+  task keeps an assignee who is no longer a member.
+- The user record itself is kept. Removing a user who has no memberships also
+  returns 204.
+
